    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0503" n="1133" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1133"/>

                <head>No. 475.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName type="from">Heep</persName>
                        to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_WH1" type="to">Hunter</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tunis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 31, 1872</date>.
                        (Received Jan. 27, 1873.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I regret to inform the Department of the
                    murder, on the night of the 24th–25th instant, of Mahmood Sennen, dragoman of
                    the United States consular agent at Bizerta.</p>
                <p>He was found, pierced with fourteen wounds and stripped of his clothing, in a
                    village near Bizerta. A considerable sum of money and several papers of value,
                    belonging to Mr. <persName>Spizzichino</persName>, the consular agent, which
                    were in charge of the dragoman, have disappeared. Four persons, brothers,
                    against whom there is strong presumptive evidence, have been arrested, and are
                    held for trial for the murder.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_GHH1">G. H. HEAP</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
